From 7685a0bf2d8799e89d3f5cfa3c5eed783b1b1019 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Corios00 <52224974+Corios00@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 14:32:41 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] The model visibility walk takes a quarter of the parts a
 frame while only the camera moves

`apply_model_visibility` skips its walk when nothing moved, but every frame the camera moves (all
of play) it re-tested every resident model part: the far wall, the distance fade, the portal and
window gates, about 100k parts in a city.

While only the camera's place or turn moved, outdoors (the window gate open, no room claimed), a
part whose own row is still is walked one frame in four, by its entity index. Its verdicts move
with the camera by a fraction of a yard a frame, and the far wall's straddlers dissolve per pixel,
so a part a few frames late reads the same. Every part is walked on any other change (a setting, a
portal, a room, the lens), when the camera is 4 yd from the last whole walk (a teleport, a
gallop's every half second), and on the first still frame after a sliced one, so no part keeps a
late verdict once the camera stops. Indoors every part is walked every frame, as the window gate
turns with the camera. `WOW_VIS_EVERY_FRAME=1` turns it off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
